  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would be inappropriately configured, with the proposed bedroom 2 at first floor now next door to the living room of the first floor flat, giving rise to impacts of harmful noise transference. The proposed development would therefore be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 D .7 of the London Plan, Policies DM1 C, DM1 D (g), DM26 A (b) and DM26 E of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 16.1px;&quot;&gt;proposal by reason of the subdivision of front garden space would interrupt the pattern and grain of development within the Christchurch Avenue street scene and furthermore,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;result in an unacceptable level of overlooking, loss of privacy and security concerns due to the low level height of the fencing between the the different flats, resulting in a compromised standard of residential amenity for future occupiers of the property.&amp;nbsp;The proposal is therefore contrary to the high quality design and residential amenity aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3.D (1)(5)(7)(10)(11) and&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1, DM2, DM26 and DM27 of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013) and the Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document (2010).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 16.1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Flat 3, due to its inadequate head height in the living room area, together with poor outlook, would result in a poor quality, cramped and unfunctional layout.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposed development due to its poor design and layout would result in a cramped, contrived,&amp;nbsp; a poor quality environment for the future occupiers of Flat 3. The proposal is therefore contrary to the high-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM26 and of the Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010) and the Mayor of London, London Plan Guidance: Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of an Insufficient Flood Risk Assessment, fails demonstrate that the proposed development would effectively manage and mitigate flood risk on site or on the adjacent properties, and that it would not create an unacceptable level of flood risk.&amp;nbsp; The proposed development would therefore be contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), policy SI 12 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1 U of Harrow Core Strategy (2012) policies DM 9 and DM10 of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
